ddraw: create a version 1 primary surface whose format cannot be a render target

Since "ddraw: Force render target bind flags on v1 swapchain candidate
surfaces." (6b486ec7830a, 2026-06), is_render_target() makes every
version 1 primary surface a render target, also without
DDSCAPS_3DDEVICE. wined3d's OpenGL adapter never gives
WINED3DFMT_P8_UINT the render target capability, so an 8-bit primary
surface requested with an explicit DDSCAPS_VIDEOMEMORY failed to be
created (without a memory flag it falls back to system memory). Diablo
II (demo 1.04, IDirectDraw, 640x480x8, DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE |
DDSCAPS_FLIP | DDSCAPS_COMPLEX | DDSCAPS_VIDEOMEMORY) stopped at start:
"Error 22: a critical error has occurred while initializing DirectDraw"
-- on any GL driver, the same with unpatched Wine 11.20 on x86-64 Linux
(llvmpipe).

ddraw_texture_init() already retries without
WINED3D_BIND_SHADER_RESOURCE when the application did not ask for a
texture; it now also retries without WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET when the
application did not ask for a 3D device (no DDSCAPS_3DDEVICE): the
surface then has no render target binding, as before that commit. A
Direct3D device still needs DDSCAPS_3DDEVICE, so nothing can render into
it. Only creations that failed take the new path.

On a Raspberry Pi 4 (V3D, OpenGL 2.1, the i386 side under Box64) the
demo now starts full screen: its menu at 800x600, a Barbarian in the Act
1 camp at 640x480, 25 frames a second (the game's own rate); the same on
x86-64 with llvmpipe. StarCraft, Heroes III, SimCity 3000, Fallout and
an 8 bpp DirectDraw test are unchanged.

--- a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
@@ -6537,7 +6537,22 @@ static HRESULT ddraw_texture_init(struct
             if (FAILED(hr = wined3d_texture_create(wined3d_device, &wined3d_desc,
                     layers, levels, WINED3D_TEXTURE_CREATE_GET_DC_LENIENT, NULL,
                     texture, &ddraw_texture_wined3d_parent_ops, &wined3d_texture)))
-                return hr;
+            {
+                /* Version 1 primary surfaces are render targets even without
+                 * DDSCAPS_3DDEVICE (see is_render_target()), but not every
+                 * format can be one: P8 never is with the OpenGL renderer.
+                 * If the user didn't explicitly ask for a 3D device, strip
+                 * WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET as well and try again. */
+                if (!(wined3d_desc.bind_flags & WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET)
+                        || (desc->ddsCaps.dwCaps & DDSCAPS_3DDEVICE))
+                    return hr;
+
+                wined3d_desc.bind_flags &= ~WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET;
+                if (FAILED(hr = wined3d_texture_create(wined3d_device, &wined3d_desc,
+                        layers, levels, WINED3D_TEXTURE_CREATE_GET_DC_LENIENT, NULL,
+                        texture, &ddraw_texture_wined3d_parent_ops, &wined3d_texture)))
+                    return hr;
+            }
         }
     }
 
